  "Distributed SQL engines such as Trino, BigQuery, Snowflake and Spark SQL turn SQL into a plan of scans, joins and aggregations spread across many workers, and reading that plan explains performance.",
  "The optimiser parses SQL into a logical plan, applies rules such as predicate pushdown and column pruning, chooses join order and strategy from table statistics, and produces a physical plan of stages. EXPLAIN shows the plan, and query profiles show actual rows, bytes and time per step. Look for full scans where you expected pruning, joins that explode row counts, huge shuffles (exchanges) and spills. Engines differ: Snowflake and BigQuery are managed warehouses with their own storage, while Trino and Athena query files in a lake through a catalog.",
